  <h2>2. Overview</h2>
  <p>
    We process personal data only as far as needed to run this website and to answer your
    inquiries. This website sets <strong>no cookies</strong>, uses <strong>no analytics or
    tracking tools</strong> and loads its fonts, scripts and media from our own server — no data
    is sent to font or tracking providers when you visit.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Hosting and server logs</h2>
  <p>
    This website is hosted on Cloudflare Pages, provided by Cloudflare, Inc., 101 Townsend St,
    San Francisco, CA 94107, USA. When you open the website, Cloudflare automatically processes
    technical data that your browser sends: IP address, date and time of the request, requested
    page, referrer, browser and operating system. We need this data to deliver the website
    securely and to defend against attacks. The legal basis is our legitimate interest in a
    secure and reliable website (Art. 6 (1) (f) GDPR). We have a data processing agreement with
    Cloudflare. Transfers to the USA are based on the EU–U.S. Data Privacy Framework and, in
    addition, on Standard Contractual Clauses (Art. 46 GDPR).
  </p>

  <h2>4. Project inquiry form</h2>
  <p>
    When you send a project inquiry, we process the data you enter: name, email address, phone
    or WhatsApp number, industry, the selected package and your message. We use this data only
    to answer your inquiry and prepare a possible project. The legal basis is Art. 6 (1) (b) GDPR
    (steps prior to entering into a contract) and Art. 6 (1) (f) GDPR (answering inquiries).
  </p>
  <p>
    The form is delivered to us by email through Resend (Resend, Inc., 2261 Market Street #5039,
    San Francisco, CA 94114, USA), which also sends you a confirmation email. Resend processes
    the data on our behalf under a data processing agreement. Transfers to the USA are based on
    Standard Contractual Clauses (Art. 46 GDPR). If the form cannot be delivered, your email
    program opens with a prepared message instead; in that case only your own email provider
    is involved.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Contact by email, phone or WhatsApp</h2>
  <p>
    If you contact us by email or phone, we process the data you give us to handle your request
    (Art. 6 (1) (b) and (f) GDPR). If you contact us through WhatsApp, WhatsApp Ireland Limited
    (Meta) also processes your data under its own privacy policy; please use email or phone if
    you do not want this.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Links to social networks</h2>
  <p>
    Our footer links to Instagram, Behance and LinkedIn. These are plain links: no data is sent to
    these networks until you click one. After that, the privacy policy of the respective network
    applies.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Storage period</h2>
  <p>
    We delete inquiry data when it is no longer needed for its purpose — usually within 12 months
    if no contract follows. If a contract follows, statutory retention periods under commercial
    and tax law apply (up to 10 years, § 257 HGB, § 147 AO).
  </p>

  <h2>8. Your rights</h2>
  <p>Under the GDPR you have the right to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>access your personal data (Art. 15),</li>
    <li>rectification (Art. 16) and erasure (Art. 17),</li>
    <li>restriction of processing (Art. 18),</li>
    <li>data portability (Art. 20),</li>
    <li>
      <strong>object</strong> to processing based on Art. 6 (1) (f) GDPR on grounds relating to
      your particular situation (Art. 21),
    </li>
    <li>withdraw any consent you gave, with effect for the future (Art. 7 (3)).</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    To use these rights, email <a href="mailto:contact@devstudiocraft.com">contact@devstudiocraft.com</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>9. Right to lodge a complaint</h2>
  <p>
    You can complain to a data protection supervisory authority. The authority responsible for
    us is: Die Landesbeauftragte für Datenschutz und Informationsfreiheit der Freien Hansestadt
    Bremen, Am Wall 153–156, 28195 Bremen.
  </p>

  <h2>10. Changes</h2>
  <p>
    We update this policy when our website or the law changes. The current version is always
    available on this page.
  </p>
